  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1016.04 Excavation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1016.04 Excavation. Any person excavating for an EDA shall:\n\n(a) Protect the natural absorption qualities of the soil;\n\n(b) Protect open excavation from storm runoff to prevent the entrance of silt and debris;\n\n(c) Rake all smeared or compacted surfaces to a depth of one inch; and\n\n(d) Remove loose material before the fill or uniform crushed stone is placed or, in the case of chambers or LDGP systems, the sand layer is constructed.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1 and #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1000) #11184, eff 10-1-16; ss by #14486, eff 2-1-26, EXPIRES: 2-1-36 (formerly Env-Wq 1016.03)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1000.html"
